What a PASS rests on
  reviewed once: FVA's specs: Wasm syntax + binary grammar, execution semantics, integer + IEEE-754 numerics, claim forms, certificate relations, the verdict rules (FVA/Spec/**)
  verified implementation: the decoder (sound + complete for the profile), the reference stepper, the float operators, instantiation, the validator (validated modules never get stuck), the verdict function, the certificate checkers (FVA.Self: fva trust on FVA itself)
  trusted glue: fact collection from the environment, the link and surface checks (a certificate's files included), process orchestration, the external kernels (each canaried)
  residual trust: the Lean kernel cross-checked by an independent kernel, the Lean compiler that built fva, Mathlib at the pinned revision, the specs
